    <!-- NO Profile TYPE, DELIBERATELY (2026-09-08). The four "GSA Standard *" /
         "GSA System Administrator" profiles were dropped from the production
         change set, so this repo no longer holds a copy of them.

         Do not re-add them to "keep the manifest complete". A profile is MERGED
         into the target org's copy rather than replacing it, so a retrieved
         profile here is a partial, already-stale snapshot of an org-wide
         component this app does not own - and listing it would sweep it into the
         next change set regenerated from this manifest.

         Sync-Metadata.ps1 only scans types that appear in this file, so removing
         this block is what keeps profiles out of the discovery report too; no
         ldgcrm-manifest-ignore.json entry is needed.

         App access is granted by the three LDGCRM_ permission sets and their
         permission set groups above. The one thing a permission set CANNOT do is
         assign a page layout - that stays a manual, per-profile step in the
         target org, done in Setup after the change set lands:
         Setup -> Profiles -> <profile> -> Page Layout Assignment -> Edit.
         Verify by opening a record as a non-admin, not by reading the profile.
         (Sprint 1's DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md, section 2c, is archived in
         archive/sprint_1_scripts.zip.) -->
    <types>
