    <!-- Backs OpportunityContactRole.Role. NOT named "OpportunityContactRole" -
         that entity does not exist and the retrieve fails. Carries the
         Day-to-Day POC / Senior POC values added for the Airtable migration.

         WARNING (2026-09-08): A RETRIEVE FROM AN ORG WHERE THOSE TWO VALUES ARE
         NOT ACTIVE SILENTLY DELETES THEM FROM THIS FILE. After the Dev refresh
         the org reports 13 active values and this file has 15.

         A retrieve returns only ACTIVE values, and a metadata deploy cannot
         delete a picklist value - it deactivates it. So "absent from the
         retrieved file" and "absent from the org" are NOT the same thing: a
         deactivated value is invisible here and to `sf sobject describe` alike,
         while still occupying its name in the value set. Check Setup (Picklist
         Value Sets -> Contact Role) before concluding a value was never there.

         That deletion looks like nothing: no warning, no error, ten fewer lines.
         It is also load-bearing - Role is part of OpportunityContactRole's
         external ID (<airtableId>|<Role>) and of the (Opportunity, Contact, Role)
         dedupe key, and Day-to-Day POC alone designates 312 of 354 primary
         contacts in the current load. Losing the values does not fail the load;
         it quietly changes which contact is primary.

         So after ANY Sync-Metadata run, check `git diff` on this file and restore
         it if the two values vanished, until the org has them. -->
    <types>
        <members>ContactRole</members>
        <name>StandardValueSet</name>
    </types>
