    <!-- External Client App (the successor to Connected Apps) for the Partner
         Portal, added 2026-09-08. ONE app in Setup is FIVE metadata components,
         each its own type with its own suffixed name - retrieving only
         ExternalClientApplication gets you a shell with no OAuth config, and
         nothing warns you. Keep all five listed together.

         The plugin settings/policies names are generated by Salesforce from the
         app's API name (_oauth, _glbloauth, _oauthPlcy, _plcy) - they are not
         free-form, so do not "tidy" them.

         ⚠️ THIS IS THE LOCAL-DEVELOPMENT APP (2026-09-08). Its callback URL is
         http://localhost:3001/auth/salesforce/callback - a Rails server on the
         developer's own machine, on the OmniAuth default path. Salesforce matches
         redirect_uri by EXACT STRING, so the path is part of the contract: a
         client redirecting to the bare origin will not match. It
         REPLACED LDGCRM_P3_Client_App, which was deleted from Dev in the same
         change - an External Client App cannot be renamed, because the API name
         is the component's identity, so "renaming" is create-new + delete-old
         and the new app carries a DIFFERENT Salesforce-generated consumer key.

         Never hand-author <consumerKey> or <oauthLink> when CREATING an app.
         Salesforce issues both, per app and per org, and carrying the old app's
         values across fails the deploy. They are present in these files now only
         because a retrieve wrote them back after the app existed.

         Before this reaches a change set for a real environment, the callback URL
         has to change - localhost is useless anywhere but a developer laptop. -->
    <types>
        <members>LDGCRM_P3_Client_app_Localdev</members>
        <name>ExternalClientApplication</name>
    </types>
    <types>
        <members>LDGCRM_P3_Client_app_Localdev_oauth</members>
        <name>ExtlClntAppOauthSettings</name>
    </types>
    <types>
        <members>LDGCRM_P3_Client_app_Localdev_glbloauth</members>
        <name>ExtlClntAppGlobalOauthSettings</name>
    </types>
    <types>
        <members>LDGCRM_P3_Client_app_Localdev_oauthPlcy</members>
        <name>ExtlClntAppOauthConfigurablePolicies</name>
    </types>
    <types>
        <members>LDGCRM_P3_Client_app_Localdev_plcy</members>
        <name>ExtlClntAppConfigurablePolicies</name>
    </types>
    <version>64.0</version>
